      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Statutory Interstate e-Way Bills, Regulatory Clearances &amp; 100% Marine Insurance for Vehicle To Transport Packers And Movers</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p>When a <strong>household relocation company in India</strong> handles your move, it must comply with a trio of statutory documents that guarantee legal compliance and protect your goods. First, the <strong>GST e‑Way bill</strong> is generated for every shipment of goods over ₹50,000, ensuring seamless customs clearance and tax audit readiness.</p>
<p>Second, the <strong>IBA‑approved Lorry Receipt (LR/Bilty)</strong> records the vehicle’s load, driver details, and destination, serving as the primary contract between the owner and the transporter. Finally, a <strong>100% declared‑value marine transit insurance</strong> under IRDAI covers accidental collisions, fire, theft, and unforeseen delays—essential for <em>vehicle transport by train</em> or <em>home from home transport</em> across long distances.</p>

<p>These documents work together to reduce risk for both the <em>home shifting agency</em> and the customer. The e‑Way bill ties the shipment to the GST framework, allowing you to claim input tax credits and avoid penalties.</p>
<p>The LR/Bilty protects against disputes over cargo quantity or condition, while the marine insurance guarantees full replacement value, even if the load is damaged during a sudden weather event or a collision on a busy highway.</p>

